## Overview

**M.O.B. (Motors on Boost)** is an aggressive arcade highway racing baseline inspired by legendary mid-2000s classics—principally *Need for Speed: Most Wanted (2005)* and *Burnout Revenge (2005)*. 

Engineered directly on top of Haxe 4.3+ and the Heaps.io framework, **M.O.B.** runs natively in modern Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit browsers via hardware-accelerated WebGL 2.0. The engine combines custom raycast vehicle dynamics, high-speed lateral drift modeling, procedural endless multi-lane highway track generation, autonomous highway traffic AI, dynamic trauma-based camera shake, and a built-in Web Audio procedural tone synthesizer into an installable Progressive Web Application (PWA).

This project represents the primary WebGL foundation of the *M.O.B.* racing line, setting the architectural foundation for upcoming sister iterations (such as the planned Godot-powered desktop title, *M.O.B. // Sektr*).

---

## Key Features

* **High-Density In-Game HUD (`InGameHUDView.hx`)**: Angled digital speedometer with gear and drifting badges, lap and race time counter, procedural real-time circuit minimap with glowing position dot and directional heading tick, curved tachometer RPM arc gauge (1k-8k RPM), curved nitro capacity arc gauge with dual-layer flame icon, and discreet real-time FPS counter.
* **Limited & Regenerating Nitrous Boost (`CarPhysics.hx`)**: Capacity model (`boostFuel`) with 0.25/s active burn consumption (4.0s sustained full boost), 0.10/s passive idle recharge, and automatic cutoff on empty.
* **Granular Steering Sensitivity (`ControlsOptionsPanel.hx` & `InputController.hx`)**: Configurable steering sensitivity setting scalable from 0% to 100% in 2% steps.
* **Decoupled 3D Render Scale (`PostProcessRenderer.hx` & `GraphicsManager.hx`)**: Independent 3D offscreen render target scaling (0.50x to 1.50x) while keeping 2D canvas and text at native 1:1 window resolution for ultra-sharp UI typography.
* **Responsive Options UI & Viewport Scrolling (`OptionsView.hx` & `GraphicsOptionsPanel.hx`)**: Scrolling menu viewport with navigation hints, adaptive card backplates, and fixed Back button hitzone avoiding tab collisions.
* **Hybrid OimoPhysics Rigid Body & Arcade Raycast Dynamics (`CarPhysics.hx`)**: OimoPhysics 3D rigid body collision backbone coupled with four-wheel independent spring-damper suspension integration along road surface normals, anti-roll bar torque distribution across wheel pairs, slip-angle cornering grip evaluated via normalized Pacejka-like curves, front vs rear tire slip bias (`tireSlipBias: [-1.0 .. 1.0]`), dedicated handbrake breakaway, automatic drift engagement at threshold slip angles (`driftTriggerAngle: 0.22 rad`), Criterion-style (*NFS: Most Wanted 2012*) counter-steer torque assist and forward velocity biasing, dynamic body roll scaling (`bodyRollScale: 1.0`), ground friction scaling (`groundFriction: 1.0`), and burnout wheelspin simulation (`wheelspinAmount: 1.2`).
* **Powertrain & Transmission Simulation**: Dynamic engine RPM flywheel calculation, progressive 6-speed gear ratios, automatic transmission up/down-shift logic, and simulated limited-slip differential (LSD).
* **Dynamic Speed Chase Camera (`ChaseCamera.hx`)**: Spring-damped target follow with controlled acceleration pull-back (+0.55m max), velocity feedforward anchoring (0.65), speed-dependent dynamic FOV (65.0° base smoothly scaling to 77.0° cruising at top speed with +3.5° boost, bounded to prevent fisheye distortion), and toned-down collision trauma dampening with rapid exponential decay (`3.8 * dt`).
* **Dual-Tier Automated Testing Infrastructure**: Headless unit test suite (`tests/`) powered by `utest` across 12 fixtures (200/200 assertions passed in under 0.06s) and automated browser testing suite (`web/test-suite.html` & `tests/run-browser-tests.js`) driven via Microsoft Edge and Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP).
* **High-Speed Radial Motion Blur (`RadialBlurShader.hx`)**: Custom HxSL screen post-processing shader with runtime `blurOrigin` and `blurIntensity` scaled dynamically with forward vehicle velocity via `PostProcessRenderer.hx`.
* **Procedural Gradient Blue Skybox (`Skybox.hx`)**: Geodesic celestial dome with custom HxSL shader blending deep azure zenith blue (`#1052B8`), bright atmospheric horizon cyan (`#7AC2F2`), and dusk nadir tones.
* **Apex Summit Solar Lighting**: Scene directional sunlight positioned at the highest south-east elevation of the circuit map (`X: +350, Y: -250, Z: 140`) providing crisp directional illumination.
* **Autonomous Highway Traffic AI**: Multi-lane procedural obstacle vehicles traversing route waypoints with dynamic spatial proximity checks, lane-following, and collision boundaries.
* **Cinematic 3-Stage Boot Sequence**: Studio, Engine, and locked Legal Disclaimer preload sequence transitioning via a 1.2-second smooth cross-fade curtain into the interactive 3D showcase.
* **Procedural Vector Iconography & PNG Asset Integration (`TouchControlsHUD.hx`, `UIIcons.hx`)**: Native loading of PNG button icons from `res/icons/` with immediate automatic fallback to resolution-independent procedural vector graphics.
* **Bumper-Navigated Glassmorphic UI**: High-contrast UI featuring edge-triggered bumper/tab navigation (`LB`/`RB` or `Q`/`E`), discrete block audio volume gauges (`■` / `□`), and real-time graphics adjustments.
* **Dual-Scheme Hardware Diagrams**: Procedural vector controller diagrams (PXN P50L / standard Xbox layouts) and keyboard diagrams with in-game button remapping and device isolation modes (`Both`, `Keyboard Only`, `Gamepad Only`).
* **Web Audio Synthesis Engine**: Custom square, sawtooth, and noise tone generators producing procedural engine RPM frequency modulation, tire screeches, and UI chime sound effects without external audio files.
* **Frosted Glass Multi-Touch Driving HUD (`TouchControlsHUD.hx`)**: Proportional virtual analog steering joystick for left thumb, left-hand Nitro button with flame icon, high-capacity Gas pad with pedal icon, disc brake pad with red caliper, and arched Drift button with native DOM TouchEvent integration and true multi-touch concurrency across all simultaneous chords.
* **State Persistence & Version Migration (`SaveSystem.hx`)**: Browser `LocalStorage` v4 schema caching for hardware graphics levels, audio channels, steering sensitivity, and mid-run race checkpoints with automated forward migration.

